Kni-Mal-Hum-Law



In my alphabetic ascension series I got to Knight role. Only seven
games were necessary to ascend a Knight and once I had a game going,
winning was only matter of time. Only quick recapitulation:



- I got a wand of wishing in my starting room (the first time I ever
got this lucky), so I wished for GDSM and charging scrolls (the wand
turned to have three inital charges)

- found coaligned altar on dlvl 2, very first sacrifice yielded
Grayswandir

- Mines and Sokoban were nominal; I got BoH and amulet of reflection;
no magic lamps

- my horse hit polytrap in the Mines, so I took some pains to turn it
into something powerful: I ended up with a winged gargoyle

- got barracks with two wands of death (one of the soldiers managed to
zap row of five of his comrades with it before I got to him)

- pet winged gargoyle was killed by another wand of death in a throne
room at dlvl 22; I got silver dragon instead, but that is so lousy
pet, that I abandoned it later (I had no magic whistle); anyway,
losing my pet was of concern, because my knight had alarmingly low HP
(approx 80), so I was bit reluctant to clear even Fort Ludios, but it
turned out not to be too much trouble due to lucky generation of
cockatrices there, so FL got its own terra cotta army

- on the Quest portal level I got room with a magic trap and an altar;
I converted the altar and "farmed" the magic trap; the trap lasted
very long time, during which I got: 4 tengus, ring of levitation,
water walking boots, Demonbane, passtune to the Castle, went from XL
13 to 14 + assorted potions and wands

- with XL 14 I embarked on the Quest; my plan was to sneak to Ixoth
and zap him with wand of polymorph before he could grab the Mirror of
Merlin; unfortunately, he took initiative into his own claws and came
to me instead, so I had to melee him
- between Medusa and Castle I found bones of post-quest Valkyrie
killed by a master mind flayer: lot of stuff, but the really important
stuff was unholy water, magic marker and another wand of death

- unfortunately, I ran into the very same 150 HP MMF who killed the
poor valkyrie, so amnesia all the way

- Castle clearing was nominal; I had still rather low HP, but I was so
efficient with two-weaponed Grayswandir and silver saber; also my
doubled magic missiles quickly dealt with pests I did not want get my
hands dirty with (rust monsters, disenchanters, mind flayers)

- cleared VotD and moved my stash there

- at Castle I got out all my 6 tengu tins and ate them -- I only got
teleportitis; so I went down to VotD to wish for a ring of teleport
control -- in a stroke of luck, I found the ring in VotD upstairs area

- after upgrading my AC and maxHP, I delved into Gehennom, which was
rather uneventful; with maxed out luck and skilled in both saber and
two-weapon combat I was slicing through the demons like a hot knife
through butter (h and L were already genocided so I was safe)

- at Vlad's I got wish from throne (all other thrones only vanished
immediately), so I wished for magic marker

- after mapping Gehennom, I had final preparations -- quite
uncharacteristically I was awash in magic markers, so I could write
charging scrolls and upgrade my AC to my heart's content -- I only got
to AC -33, since this looked like more than enough -- in hind sight,
I'd certainly get more next time

- I killed Rodney, performed the ritual and levelported into the
Sanctum, I did not use jumping and in the beginning not even conflict
and I was surprised how quickly my hit points vanish; I expected
things to be easier with my high AC; I put on conflict, slew the high
priest and rose through the ceiling and begin the run to the Planes

- mysterious force was annoying to the max; when I was ascending
lawful Caveman, it only kicked only twice, but this time I was moving
up very slowly; also, wands of death kept missing Rodney way too often

- in the Planes, I got some uneasy moments with hordes of air
elementals in my back, some of which managed to engulf me and shave
good deal of my hit points - I had to use my only wand of
teleportation; on the Plane of Water I had (for the first time) quite
a trouble finding the portal (but I was in no danger since ; were
genocided anyway)

- on the Astral Plane, I was lucky and did not need to confront any
Rider and the first altar was the right one


All in all, Knight seems like an easy role to me. I don't know if my
low HP increase was an anomaly, but apart from that, there are many
advantages: good early weapon, chance of getting Grayswandir from
sacrifice, good quest artifact making magic missile quite powerful,
generally excellent spellcasting (too bad I never found any healing
spellbook).


